From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:13:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: keep the AGX bit out of the
 export, document clearing

apple_pmp_report_set_request() lets a client outside pmp-report update one
bit of the PS-REQ word. On the T6001 bit 9 is the AGX request, which the
GPU vote owns: a second writer could clear it while the GPU works, or set
it and leave it set. Refuse it from the export with -EBUSY on a t600x
report. The vote itself writes through apple_pmp_report_set_state() and is
not affected.

Document what a caller must do after -ETIMEDOUT: the request was written
but not acknowledged and stays in the word, so the caller clears it with
@enable false and @no_ack true before giving up.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit e033631c7dddcd8cd47b8efde090d0ac3e7e9a5e)
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 56eb082909..d5823dd3d2 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -1558,12 +1558,13 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_report_set_t6030_gfx);
  * returned, as for a report entry.
  *
  * The caller owns the bit it requests; this function does not arbitrate between callers of the
- * same bit. On the T6001 bit 9 belongs to the AGX vote (pmp_report.agx_vote), so other callers
- * must not use it.
+ * same bit. On the T6001 bit 9 belongs to the AGX vote (pmp_report.agx_vote) and is refused here
+ * with -EBUSY. After -ETIMEDOUT the request was written but not acknowledged and stays in the
+ * word: the caller must clear it (@enable false, @no_ack true) before giving up.
  *
  * Context: process context (the acknowledge wait is a busy poll of up to 50 ms).
  * Return: 0, -ENODEV if no report is bound to @report_np, -EINVAL if @id is out of range,
- * -ETIMEDOUT if the acknowledge did not follow.
+ * -EBUSY for the T6001 AGX bit, -ETIMEDOUT if the acknowledge did not follow.
  */
 int apple_pmp_report_set_request(const struct device_node *report_np, unsigned int id,
 				bool enable, bool no_ack)
@@ -1576,7 +1577,10 @@ int apple_pmp_report_set_request(const struct device_node *report_np, unsigned i
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	list_for_each_entry_rcu(rep, &apple_pmp_reports, list) {
 		if (rep->dev->of_node == report_np) {
-			ret = apple_pmp_report_set_state(rep, id, enable, no_ack);
+			if (id == APPLE_PMP_T6001_AGX_ID && rep->offsets == &apple_pmp_offsets_t600x)
+				ret = -EBUSY;	/* the AGX vote owns this bit */
+			else
+				ret = apple_pmp_report_set_state(rep, id, enable, no_ack);
 			break;
 		}
 	}
